#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""arty: reference tooling for the project console.

Subcommands, no dependencies beyond the standard library:

  init      write the .arty pointer and the meta/project seed for a new console
  page      emit the console HTML on stdout, for the agent to publish
  sync      reconcile a console database dump against the repository: build the
            snapshot (git graph, features, the whole docky tree), recompute map
            staleness, and write a batch plan of the rows that changed
  snapshot  write the snapshot as one JSON file, for a local look at the page
  due       say whether the console is behind the repository (a Stop hook)
  check     validate a console database dump against the schema

Nothing here talks to claude.ai, and nothing here knows anything about a
particular project. The agent carries the rows (read_db --out_dir in, write_db
batch out); this script owns git, the schema and the page. Every
project-specific fact lives in the database.

If this script ever needs to test a project by name, the schema is
underspecified -- fix the schema, not this file.

See SKILL.md for the schema itself; section references below point into it.
"""
